      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The Problem is that once people would find it, they would start using it without actually knowing stuff would break because of it. I've already seen a lot of Avatars breaking from it (my own included) which is also why I haven't really used the feature yet, because I don't want peoples Avatars to break. This could also lead to situations where for someone the Avatar is working fine and for someone else it's broken etc. Or getting told by someone that their animations aren't working, without knowing that the Avatar Hider of that person caused it.\nI don't think having this as an option would be the right thing to do, it should be uniform and the same for everyone to ensure it works correctly.\nI would much rather have them looking in to ways where they could solve this problem rather then to just give us an option to ignore it and break stuff. I do wonder if there are ways where they could basically \"pause / unpause\" animators without having to turn them off / on. Or ways for them to save the defaults. \nWe have to see what they come up with or if they decide that just not touching animators at all with the Avatar Hider is the way to go.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
